    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "**Is this car safe?**\r\n\r\nThousands of parts go into a car. Factories have quality inspections, which either pass or fail these parts. A pass rate that’s lower than 95% might indicate a factory isn’t doing a good job. \r\n\r\nUse Python to analyze a factory’s inspections.\r\n\r\n☑️ Do This:\r\n- Count the number of \"Passed\" and \"Failed\" inspections in the \"status\" column of `data.csv`.\r\n- Interpret the data: Should this factory be trusted? Be ready to share your thoughts on the next level.",
